{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"experiment": "E003", "refs": ["EXPERIMENTS/007-build-timestamps/results.json", "FAILURES-claims.md"], "summary": "Build-timestamp census over 200 PyPI wheels drawn from 10 declared packages (T-0013, EXPERIMENTS/007-build-timestamps/). Gate metric non_1980_fraction 0.965 (95% CI 0.940-0.990) against RESEARCH/E.md's 5% threshold, so the declared gate passes at 19x and the verdict is lead-survives. Stricter lower bounds beside it: violation_fraction 0.670 of wheels with disagreeing entry dates, carried_mtime_fraction 0.145 spanning an hour or more, widest requests-2.26.0 at 23 entries over 789 days. Zero of 200 wheels carried a unix-epoch integer in METADATA or RECORD, so the mechanism's embedded-string assumption is half false. Zero failures over 205,305,241 bytes; numbers identical across three consecutive runs. The declared metric measures DOS-epoch pinning rather than reproducibility and nothing was rebuilt, so no cause is attributed: recorded as FAILURES.md F009, attribution deferred to T-0016 (EXPERIMENTS/008-build-timestamp-attribution/)."}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "experiment_result", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 17, "session": "2026-10-03-026-run-e3-s-build-timestamp-census-over-200", "ts": "2026-10-03T21:26:40+00:00"}
